  "question": {
    "text": "The open-chain glucose, (an aldohexose) and fructose (a 2-oxohexose) have X and Y chiral carbons respectively. Find the sum of X + Y."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Open-chain glucose,<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0017_8d051ea95ef1.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 111px; height: 157px;\" />&nbsp;and open-chain fructose,<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0017_a75b70f24120.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 114px; height: 168px;\" />&nbsp;has three chiral carbons.<br />Hence sum of X + Y = 4 + 3 = 7."
